WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
Text on an ivory background, read aloud: "A screenshot isn't a rent record."

00:03.200 --> 00:08.400
Tenant101 on a phone with demo data. The tenant's home shows Unit 101 with a balance of ₱81,675, marked as still owed. "With Tenant101, every tenant sees their balance, right on their phone."

00:08.400 --> 00:15.000
The tenant taps Pay this rental. Sped up twice, the amount 16,500 and the reference DEMO-0925-4471 are typed and a receipt is attached. "To pay, they report the transfer, with its reference and receipt."

00:15.000 --> 00:17.667
The tenant taps Submit; the app confirms "Payment submitted".

00:17.667 --> 00:21.667
Back home, Unit 101 still shows ₱81,675. "It doesn't count yet. The balance waits for the landlord."

00:21.667 --> 00:28.467
On the landlord's phone, the report shows ₱16,500 with its reference; the landlord approves: "Payment recorded. Receipt #152 issued." "The landlord checks the report, and approves it."

00:28.467 --> 00:31.967
The tenant's Unit 101 balance now reads ₱65,175. "Only then does the balance change."

00:31.967 --> 00:35.967
The lion mark. "Tenant101. Who's paid, and what's next." See how it works at tommydeleon.com. Team project, not launched, demo data.
